5417] [17592186501097 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501097 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186500592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501097 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b07d72d2-93c7-594a-8963-dcc12be62f0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501104 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501104 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501104 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501104 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186500523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501104 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bb588555-9fd1-5660-8555-bc1960f97262" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501183 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501183 #edb/ref 1069 "q-89606" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501183 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501183 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{75}x,\\, & 5\\le x\\le 10 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<5 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 5\\le x\\le 10 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501183 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "770dc96c-77d3-556b-b303-18d387043365" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501183 #edb/ref 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $5\\le x\\le 10,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<5 \\\\ {\\int }_{5}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 5\\le x\\le 10 \\\\ 1, & x>10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{5}^{x}\\frac{2}{75}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{75}{t}^{2}|}_{5}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{75}{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-25}{75}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<5, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-25}{75},\\, & 5\\le x\\le 10, \\\\ 1,\\, & x>10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501212 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501212 #edb/ref 1069 "q-89634" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501212 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501212 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\pi (1+{x}^{6})},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nfind the cumulative distribution function $F(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501212 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b31007d2-c9e1-51d3-8e66-44402735c224" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501212 #edb/ref 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{\\pi (1+{t}^{6})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({t}^{3})}{\\pi }|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501225 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501225 #edb/ref 1069 "q-185531" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501225 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501225 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{e}^{-|x|}}{2},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2},\\, & x\\le 0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501225 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d0e0e171-2942-5666-9f4c-984a9e7d868a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501225 #edb/ref 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}\\,\\text{d}t, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{2}\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x\\le 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{2}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{2}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2},\\, & x\\le 0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2},\\, & x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501252 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186501283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501252 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1943e8ec-2299-593e-84f2-5af6e5f545e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501252 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186500293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501258 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186501263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] 